---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base>
  {/* ===== Hero ===== */}
  <section class="container py-24 sm:py-32">
    <p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg-subtle mb-8 tracking-wide lowercase">
      apache 2.0 · audit-ledger-first · v1 ships june 16
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-[2.5rem] sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl lg:text-7xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.05] text-fg hero-shine">
      Predictive reliability for AI agents.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-8 text-lg sm:text-xl text-fg-muted max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      Rust gateway across 35 providers. Full-fidelity OTel observability. Predictive pre-flight guardrails enforce policy at the gateway, p99 sub-50ms. Every span signed, Merkle-chained, anchored to Sigstore Rekor.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
      <a href="#notify" class="btn-primary lowercase">get notified at launch</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/tracelane" class="btn-secondary lowercase" rel="me noopener">
        follow on github →
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-fg-subtle font-mono lowercase">
      v1 ships tue jun 16, 2026 · no credit card required for free hosted tier
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ===== What it is ===== */}
  <section id="what" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">
      What Tracelane is.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted max-w-2xl">
      Three integrated surfaces in one developer interface. Open core. Apache 2.0.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-3">
      <article>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mb-3 lowercase tracking-wider">01 — gateway</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Universal LLM gateway</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          35 providers. One canonical wire format. Rust + Axum + tokio. p99 overhead under 25ms at 5K RPS single-node. BYOK only — provider keys envelope-encrypted, never in logs.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mb-3 lowercase tracking-wider">02 — observability</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Full-fidelity traces</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          OTel GenAI semconv on every span. ClickHouse hot tier (90 days). Cloudflare R2 cold tier (forever). Time-travel replay of any past trace. No sampling, no truncation — full fidelity.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mb-3 lowercase tracking-wider">03 — guardrails</p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Predictive layer</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          12 predictors run inline before the gateway forwards. Sub-50ms p99 on Hetzner CCX13 CPU. Flags poisoned MCP tools, infinite loops, cost runaways, PII leaks, jailbreak attempts in the predictive pre-flight pass. Fail-open with configurable timeout.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Migration ===== */}
  <section id="migrate" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">
      Migrating from a tool that got acquired or breached?
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted max-w-2xl">
      Two CLI commands at V1. No data leaves your infrastructure during migration.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-8 lift-card">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg">From Helicone</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          16,000 organizations stranded after the Mintlify acquisition (Mar 2026).
        </p>
        <pre class="mt-6 rounded bg-bg-subtle p-4 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto text-fg"><code>$ tlane import-helicone \
    --source-url $HELICONE_URL \
    --source-key $HELICONE_KEY</code></pre>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          Migrates traces, configs, prompts, and rate-limit rules. ~5 minutes for a 1M-span account.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-8 lift-card">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-fg">From LiteLLM</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          After CVE-2026-33634 (Mar 24) and CVE-2026-42208 (Apr 24).
        </p>
        <pre class="mt-6 rounded bg-bg-subtle p-4 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto text-fg"><code>$ tlane import-litellm \
    --config litellm_config.yaml</code></pre>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          Drop-in gateway replacement. Sigstore-signed releases. SLSA Build L3 provenance. Trusted Publishing OIDC — no long-lived tokens.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Audit ledger ===== */}
  <section id="audit" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mb-4 tracking-wider lowercase">the audit ledger</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight max-w-3xl text-fg leading-[1.1]">
      Every span. Cryptographically signed.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-fg-muted max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      Every trace event is Ed25519-signed, Merkle-chained, and anchored to
      <a href="https://docs.sigstore.dev/logging/overview/" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors" rel="noopener">Sigstore Rekor</a>
      within 60 seconds. Tampering with the audit log requires breaking SHA-256, Ed25519, or the public Rekor witness — not your customer's KMS.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">eu ai act</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          Article 12 export pack — full audit trail for high-risk AI systems. Annex III enforcement deferred to Dec 2, 2027 (Digital Omnibus, May 7, 2026); audit ledger ships at V1.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">india dpdp</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          Phase II enforcement Nov 13, 2026. Region-pinned storage. Audit log retention configurable.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">hipaa</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          BAA available on Business tier. PII redaction inline. Provider keys envelope-encrypted.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <pre class="mt-12 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-6 font-mono text-sm overflow-x-auto text-fg"><code><span class="text-fg-subtle"># verify any trace anchored to Sigstore Rekor</span>
$ tlane verify trace_2026_06_16_abc123
✓ signature valid (Ed25519)
✓ Merkle chain unbroken (depth 14)
✓ Rekor log entry 18234567 — anchored 2026-06-16T08:14:22Z
✓ tamper-evident: yes</code></pre>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Pricing ===== */}
  <section id="pricing" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Pricing.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted max-w-2xl">
      Open core. Self-host free forever. Hosted tiers start at $0.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-6 lift-card">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-fg">OSS self-host</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-3xl text-fg">$0</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-subtle">Apache 2.0 · forever</p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          <li>Full Rust gateway · 35 providers</li>
          <li>ClickHouse + R2 storage</li>
          <li>DuckDB embedded option (Lite)</li>
          <li>Community Discord support</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-6 lift-card">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-fg">Free hosted</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-3xl text-fg">$0</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-subtle">1M spans / mo</p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          <li>Single workspace, 1 seat</li>
          <li>30-day trace retention</li>
          <li>5 predictors enabled</li>
          <li>No credit card</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-6 lift-card">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-fg">Builder</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-3xl text-fg">
          $59<span class="text-base text-fg-muted">/mo</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-subtle">25M spans / mo · 3 seats</p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          <li>90-day retention</li>
          <li>All 12 predictors</li>
          <li>Predictive pre-flight history (read-only)</li>
          <li>Email support · 24h</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-md border-2 border-fg bg-bg-elevated p-6 relative lift-card glow-pulse">
        <p class="absolute -top-3 left-6 px-2 bg-bg-elevated text-xs font-mono text-fg lowercase">recommended</p>
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-fg">Team</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-3xl text-fg">
          $249<span class="text-base text-fg-muted">/mo</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-subtle">100M spans / mo · unlimited seats</p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          <li>180-day retention</li>
          <li>Predictive pre-flight + tamper-evident promotion record</li>
          <li>WorkOS SSO</li>
          <li>Slack support · 8h</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-6 lift-card">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-fg">Business</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-3xl text-fg">
          $899<span class="text-base text-fg-muted">/mo</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-subtle">500M spans / mo</p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          <li>1-year retention</li>
          <li>SOC 2 Type II artifacts</li>
          <li>Cedar policy framework</li>
          <li>Dedicated Slack · 4h</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-6 lift-card">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-fg">Enterprise</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-3xl text-fg">
          $2,999+<span class="text-base text-fg-muted">/mo</span>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-subtle">Custom volume</p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
          <li>Unlimited retention</li>
          <li>Region pinning (US / EU / IN)</li>
          <li>BYOK + CMK self-service</li>
          <li>1h SLA · dedicated CSM</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-md border border-border-strong bg-bg-elevated p-6">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4">
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-wrap">
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-fg">Tamper-evident agent ledger</h3>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider px-2 py-0.5 border border-border-strong rounded-sm">ships at v1</span>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">
            $999/mo add-on. Cryptographic audit ledger ships at V1 — Ed25519-signed, Merkle-chained, Sigstore Rekor anchored. EU AI Act Article 12 export pack, India DPDP Phase II compliance pack, and HIPAA BAA available at V1. EU AI Act Annex III enforcement deferred to Dec 2, 2027 (Digital Omnibus, May 7, 2026).
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="font-mono text-2xl text-fg shrink-0">
          +$999<span class="text-base text-fg-muted">/mo</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-12 text-center text-sm text-fg-subtle">
      Core tiers available at V1 launch · Tue Jun 16, 2026
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Trust signals ===== */}
  <section id="trust" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mb-4 tracking-wider lowercase">security posture</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">
      Built for procurement reviews.
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-5 lift-card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">release integrity</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          Sigstore Cosign keyless signing. SLSA Build L3 provenance. Trusted Publishing OIDC — no long-lived tokens.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-5 lift-card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">sbom</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          CycloneDX SBOM published with every release. Verifiable from GitHub release artifacts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-5 lift-card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">vuln scanning</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          OSV-Scanner + Grype + Syft on every commit. Trivy explicitly banned (CVE-2026-33634).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-5 lift-card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">containers</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          Chainguard Wolfi base images only. Distroless. No shell.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-5 lift-card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">transport</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          TLS 1.3 minimum. mTLS via SPIFFE/SPIRE for ingest. SSRF defense — RFC1918 + link-local denied.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-5 lift-card">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim lowercase tracking-wider">standards</p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-muted">
          OTel GenAI semconv contributor.
          <code class="font-mono text-xs">gen_ai.guardrail.decision</code>
          event proposed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-fg-muted">
      Full security posture:
      <a href="/security" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors">/security</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  {/* ===== FAQ ===== */}
  <section id="faq" class="container py-24 border-t border-border">
    <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">Frequently asked.</h2>

    <div class="mt-16 space-y-8 max-w-3xl">
      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          What is Tracelane?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          Tracelane is an open-source (Apache 2.0) reliability platform for AI agents that combines a universal Rust LLM gateway, full-fidelity OpenTelemetry observability, and sub-50ms predictive guardrails. Every trace event is Ed25519-signed and anchored to Sigstore Rekor for cryptographic audit-log integrity.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          How is Tracelane different from Helicone, LangSmith, or Langfuse?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          Tracelane unifies the gateway, observability, predictive guardrail, and tamper-evident audit ledger in one Rust binary. Helicone, Langfuse, and LangSmith are observability-first — you bring your own gateway and your own guardrails. Tracelane is Apache 2.0 core with a published self-host path; Helicone's gateway is GPL-3.0 (corporate-procurement-hostile), Arize Phoenix is ELv2 (no SaaS resale), and LangSmith is closed-source. Tracelane's audit ledger anchors to Sigstore Rekor — no competitor in this category offers cryptographic audit log integrity at the trace level.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          What about LangSmith Engine?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          LangSmith Engine (May 13, 2026) clusters production failures after they happen and drafts pull requests to fix them. Tracelane's predictive pre-flight guardrails flag the same failure modes at the gateway before the call reaches the provider — sub-50ms p99 on commodity CPU. Engine is locked to the LangSmith trace surface and LangChain-managed inference keys per LangChain's terms of service; Tracelane is neutral OTel ingest with 0% BYOK markup across 35 providers. Different layer of the agent reliability stack. <a href="/vs/langsmith-engine" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors">Detailed comparison →</a>
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          Is Tracelane really open source?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          Yes. The core (Rust gateway, ingest workers, observability backend, predictive layer, CLI, SDKs, audit verifiers) is Apache 2.0. The
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">/ee</code> directory contains
          Tracelane Enterprise License code (paid-tier features behind entitlements). The
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">/spec</code>
          directory is CC0. The license boundary is enforced via the workspace_entitlements table — paid features are gated at the application layer, not by license-string compare.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          Which providers does Tracelane support?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          At V1: 35 providers including Anthropic, OpenAI, Google Gemini, AWS Bedrock, Together, Fireworks, Groq, OpenRouter, DeepSeek, xAI, Mistral, Azure OpenAI, Vertex AI, and 22 more. Single canonical wire format across all of them.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          Does Tracelane support EU AI Act Article 12?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          The Tamper-Evident Agent Ledger add-on ($999/mo) ships at V1 launch June 16, 2026. The cryptographic audit ledger (Ed25519-signed, Merkle-chained, Sigstore Rekor anchored), EU AI Act Article 12 export pack, India DPDP Phase II compliance pack, and HIPAA BAA are all available at V1. EU AI Act Annex III high-risk obligations were originally scheduled for Aug 2, 2026; the Digital Omnibus political agreement (May 7, 2026) deferred enforcement to Dec 2, 2027. The ledger ships now so regulated buyers can run on it under voluntary commitments and have years of audit history in place before binding enforcement.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          What's the latency overhead?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          Gateway overhead p50 &lt;5ms, p95 &lt;15ms, p99 &lt;25ms (excluding provider time). Predictive guardrail layer inline p50 &lt;30ms, p99 &lt;50ms on Hetzner CCX13 CPU. Measured numbers will be published as the Tracelane Reliability Benchmark v1.0 at V1 launch.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          Can I self-host?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          Yes. Docker Compose for development, Helm chart for production. Runs on a $5/mo VPS for the Lite (DuckDB embedded) configuration. Full ClickHouse + R2 production setup runs on a single Hetzner CCX13 ($15/mo). See
          <a href="https://docs.tracelane.dev" class="underline decoration-fg-subtle hover:decoration-fg transition-colors" rel="noopener">docs.tracelane.dev</a>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="border-b border-border pb-6 group">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between text-fg">
          When does V1 launch?
          <span class="text-fg-dim group-open:rotate-45 transition-transform">+</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
          Tuesday, June 16, 2026 at 8:00 AM ET (5:30 PM IST) on Hacker News Show HN, X, LinkedIn, and Bluesky simultaneously. Get on the notification list above.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ===== Notify form ===== */}
  <section id="notify" class="container py-24 border-t border-border bg-bg-elevated/30">
    <div class="max-w-2xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg">
        Get the V1 launch email.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted">
        One email on June 16. Then nothing unless you opt into product updates. No newsletter, no marketing automation.
      </p>
      <form id="notify-form" class="mt-8 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3" method="POST" action="/api/notify">
        <label for="email" class="sr-only">email address</label>
        <input
          id="email"
          type="email"
          name="email"
          required
          autocomplete="email"
          placeholder="you@company.com"
          class="flex-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm text-fg placeholder:text-fg-dim focus:outline-none focus:border-fg-subtle"
        />
        <button type="submit" class="btn-primary lowercase">notify me</button>
      </form>
      <p id="notify-status" class="mt-4 text-sm text-fg-subtle min-h-[1.25rem]" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    const form = document.getElementById("notify-form");
    const status = document.getElementById("notify-status");
    if (!form || !status) return;

    form.addEventListener("submit", async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const emailInput = document.getElementById("email");
      const submitBtn = form.querySelector("button[type='submit']");
      if (!emailInput || !submitBtn) return;

      const email = emailInput.value.trim();
      status.textContent = "Sending...";
      submitBtn.disabled = true;

      try {
        const res = await fetch("/api/notify", {
          method: "POST",
          body: JSON.stringify({ email }),
          headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        });
        if (res.ok) {
          status.textContent = "You're on the list. See you June 16.";
          form.reset();
        } else {
          const data = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
          status.textContent = data.error || "Something went wrong. Try again.";
        }
      } catch {
        status.textContent = "Network error. Try again.";
      } finally {
        submitBtn.disabled = false;
      }
    });
  })();
</script>
